DEVOPS PRACTICAL 1 — DOCKER

1. INSTALL / CHECK DOCKER
Install Docker Desktop for Windows.

Open VS Code Terminal / CMD:
docker --version
Expected:
Docker version XX.X.X
  
2. CHECK DOCKER
docker info

3. PULL NGINX IMAGE
docker pull nginx

4. VIEW DOCKER IMAGES
docker images
Expected:
nginx

5. RUN NGINX CONTAINER
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx
  
Open browser:
http://localhost:8080
Expected:
Welcome to nginx!

6. VIEW RUNNING CONTAINERS
docker ps

7. STOP CONTAINER
First get the container ID:
docker ps
Then:
docker stop <container-id>
Example:
docker stop abc123
  
8. FINAL COMMAND FLOW
docker --version
       ↓
docker info
       ↓
docker pull nginx
       ↓
docker images
       ↓
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx
       ↓
http://localhost:8080
       ↓
docker ps
       ↓
docker stop <container-id>
